            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:agent-before-used-at"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server/src/warden_server/api/agents.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 79,
                  "startLine": 68
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Concurrent enrollment can reuse a one-time token\n\nThe enrollment endpoint checks `used_at` and marks the token used in separate ORM steps, so two concurrent requests with the same valid token can both pass the one-time-token check before either transaction commits.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Race condition\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-362\n\nRemediation:\nClaim enrollment tokens atomically, for example with `UPDATE enrollment_tokens SET used_at = :now WHERE token_hash = :hash AND used_at IS NULL AND expires_at >= :now RETURNING id`, then create the agent only if exactly one row was claimed. Alternatively, select the row `FOR UPDATE` in PostgreSQL and re-check before creating the agent.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Add a PostgreSQL integration test that sends concurrent enrollment requests with the same token and asserts exactly one succeeds.\n- Assert that sequential reuse still returns 400 after the atomic claim change.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Keep one-time credential state transitions in database-atomic operations rather than application read-check-write sequences."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:3fe99de10cdfdc87d692a4e1c6281c4786a8ddf98a85dd56aefc18833cfb8670"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "race-condition",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_3aa760497e45b69f4ac9bce2",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_f62fd76659ce64d038a91ab6",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "race.enrollment-token-reuse",
          "ruleIndex": 2
        }
      ],
